    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 48 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS, including the new `Cp35Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created, and flagged so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32) as read-only properties on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and the mapper exposes them on GET.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added persisted `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns with getters/setters.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the two columns to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`DetectPossibleDuplicate`** (new OfficeFloor function) \u2014 runs after `BuildOwner` (owner has normalized telephone, lastName, postcode) and only for owners that already passed the hard-duplicate `EnsureUniqueIdentity` check. It scans existing owners for one sharing `lastName` + `postcode` with a different telephone (lowest id when several match), setting the flag and match id, else `false`.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `possibleDuplicate` step into the pipeline before `save` (under the same `transaction` governance).\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `ignore = true` mappings for the two new read-only fields on the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping, consistent with the other derived fields.\n\nThe rule keys off the normalized/stored telephone and postcode, so it composes correctly with the existing telephone-normalization and postcode-validation steps that run earlier in the pipeline.",
